On 2026-10-10, the reusable Create Set browser surface began admitting
the existing extension host's exact `requireMetadataConfirmation: true`
acknowledgement after a single possible Save Set click. A lost injected
script reply can now proceed to independent saved-title/description
observation, but never causes a second submission or a fabricated receipt.
Synthetic tests prove both successful verification and an inconclusive
read-back preserve the single-click guarantee.

On 2026-10-10, durable set receipts, checkpoint restoration, and
checkpoint advancement began enforcing the same bounded opaque remote-set
ID contract as Blooket set reads. Previously an adapter could persist a
nonempty but oversized or control-bearing ID that downstream browser reads
and writes would always reject. Portable tests verify invalid IDs fail
before a receipt becomes a durable remote target.

On 2026-10-10, the journaled verification boundary stopped translating
a generic `not-confirmed` verifier verdict into automatic attempt cleanup.
Only positive provider evidence can advance this read-only reconciliation
path: negative labels are still inconclusive because delayed writes cannot
be ruled out by a bounded browser observation. Explicit, separately
supported reconciliation remains available for independently established
negative evidence; portable tests protect the pending journal.

On 2026-10-10, canonical publication tests also began enforcing
that an unchanged collection during an uncertain Create Set does not
release the journal, authorize a subsequent publication step, or allow
an application update. Former tests assumed the opposite and would have
allowed a delayed provider save to race a duplicate retry. The full
portable suite passes with the stricter recovery requirement.

On 2026-10-10, differential Create Set and Add Question reconciliation
began requiring two independently read, identical positive collections
before confirming a pending attempt. Create Set also repeats the saved
metadata detail probe. A transient post-submit card or a concurrently edited
detail therefore remains inconclusive instead of advancing the durable
checkpoint. Portable regressions cover disappearing candidates and changed
saved descriptions.

On 2026-10-10, unchanged My Sets and question collections stopped
counting as negative proof of an ambiguous write. A provider save may
become visible only after its first post-submit read; clearing the journal
at that point could authorize a duplicate retry. Synthetic delayed-visibility
checks show reconciliation remains pending until an exact positive
collection difference appears, then advances the original journal.

On 2026-10-10, the portable Create Set browser surface began requiring
exact host acknowledgements at Open, Prepare, Submit, and saved-receipt
observation boundaries. Previously a truthy malformed success could trigger
the next mutation step, while an extra-field receipt could become a reported
set ID. Synthetic regressions reject malformed intermediate and final host
replies without treating them as saved provider state.

On 2026-10-10, the reusable text Create Set browser surface began
forwarding the exact submitted title and description to its separate remote
observation call. Previously that composition admitted a host receipt
without even providing the expected saved metadata. Synthetic surface tests
verify forwarding and reject a mismatched persisted-detail confirmation.

On 2026-10-10, persisted write execution began validating the exact
mutation-pacing lease and cancellation envelopes before any further work.
Previously a truthy but malformed pacer reply could skip lease acquisition
while still proceeding to reserve budget, journal an attempt, and mutate.
Synthetic tests verify unknown codes, missing release methods, and malformed
lease timestamps stop before mutation or durable attempt creation.

On 2026-10-10, explicit reconciliation began requiring exact
`not-confirmed` and `confirmed` resolution envelopes. Previously the public
reconciliation entrypoint could accept a negative result with extra or
contradictory fields and clear an ambiguous attempt. Portable tests verify
that malformed resolutions preserve the pending journal and its recovery
evidence instead of making a write eligible for immediate replay.

On 2026-10-10, the final write-execution port began validating exact
confirmed receipts and known browser stops before advancing a checkpoint.
Previously a truthy acknowledgement from an unexpected adapter could be
trusted as a typed write result; forged provider fields were not checked
at this final boundary. Portable tests prove malformed results cannot
advance an unjournaled operation and leave persisted attempts ambiguous
rather than confirming them or allowing immediate replay.

On 2026-10-10, baseline capture began validating the outer runtime
response before pacing, mutation-budget reservation, or attempt journaling.
Previously a truthy status or a surface failure with extra fields could be
admitted as a typed baseline result, even though baseline contents were
already decoded strictly. Portable tests reject malformed first and second
captures and verify no remote write or new attempt follows.

On 2026-10-10, verifier result admission now rejects unknown outcomes,
extra response fields, invalid receipt kinds, and unrecognized browser stops
before touching an ambiguous persisted attempt. Previously an unknown
outcome could fall through to `not-confirmed`, clearing the journal and
making a duplicate retry possible. Synthetic recovery tests verify that the
attempt and checkpoint remain unchanged for malformed responses.

The same pass tightened the set-list, set-detail, and question-list verifier
read envelopes. Inner IR decoding was already strict, but truthy `ok`
lookalikes or unexpected outer fields could previously reach reconciliation.
Synthetic tests now reject these replies without creating confirmation.

On 2026-10-10, the canonical browser-write adapter began enforcing exact
runtime envelopes for Create Set and Add Question confirmations and stops.
Previously a structurally extra or malformed internal surface result could be
accepted based on a truthy `ok` property, or propagated into durable attempt
